Package: mica-gce-agent
Version: 0.0.1-1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1794096000
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mica build <mica@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Mica OS agent for SSH logins on Google Compute Engine
 Follows the instance's and the project's ssh-keys metadata, which gcloud
 compute ssh and the console's SSH button write: keeps a login account
 (mica-accounts' login class, in its admin group while micad grants it) and a
 key file in /run/mica/authorized-keys for each user they name, never root or
 mica, and removes both when the user's keys leave the metadata or expire; the
 home on DATA stays. Honours block-project-ssh-keys and enable-oslogin.
 Carries a systemd unit and an OpenRC script and enables neither: a Compute
 Engine product enables it.
